To sum up: if you don't get the timing right on descending the stairs (I
know in principle how to get it right, but still often seem to miss the
right turn), Demogorgon will have at least one chance to stun you with
your approach, which may be fatal. Because then you cannot immediately
write Elbereth and he can sicken and stun you the next turn again, plus
take off your hit points fast. Since after two illness attacks, you
should at least heal the illness, you may have major difficulties to get
into a state of not being stunned and write the E-word. (Of course, you
could carry a scroll of scare monster in your inventory to avoid that
problem.) This may rarely lead to being killed, but a 2% chance as
suggested would correspond to a rare event...

With my approach, he never can touch you after you descend the stairs,
so stunning is not an issue. You can take your time to kill him at a
distance. And you need the E-word at most once (not twice), so it is
easier to replace it with a scroll of scare monster. Moreover, since
cursed scrolls of earth are rare, you don't need to waste a potion of
unholy water with my approach.


